# Spec 06 Phase A — Packing plan engine + daily-dose integration (CORE)
#
# ACCEPTANCE CONTRACT (written before build)
# A1 GIVEN inventory rooms with storage, general, guest, garage, secondary-bedroom,
#    kitchen, primary-bedroom, and bathroom items, WHEN a plan is generated, THEN
#    sessions follow the LOCKED category order and the first-night bag is last/standalone.
# A2 GIVEN a move date and enough calendar days, WHEN the plan is generated, THEN
#    sessions are reverse-scheduled through moveDate-1 with no dropped session.
# A3 GIVEN fewer calendar days than sessions, WHEN the plan is generated, THEN the
#    smallest adjacent non-first-night sessions merge until the timeline fits (except
#    the documented one-day/standalone-bag edge) and no item summary is dropped.
# A4 GIVEN past-dated incomplete sessions, WHEN the plan loads, THEN remaining work is
#    silently re-spread from today through moveDate-1 and at most one due packing task
#    is selected into a day's frozen dose.
# A5 GIVEN a submitted inventory review, WHEN submitFinal succeeds, THEN
#    users/{uid}/packingPlan/current exists and PACKING_SESSION_n task docs materialize.
# A6 GIVEN a completed packing session, WHEN the user completes its view, THEN the task
#    and plan session complete atomically, the locked consequence line renders, and the
#    next incomplete session remains scheduled.
# A7 GIVEN a move-date change or inventory resubmission, WHEN regeneration runs, THEN
#    sessions matching stable session keys preserve completedAt.
# A8 GIVEN the Phase A diff, WHEN unit tests and an iPhone 17 Pro simulator build/run are
#    executed by a fresh-context validator, THEN every criterion receives PASS/FAIL with evidence.
#
# NEEDS-CLARIFICATION (bounded, reversible interpretations)
# - Firestore shorthand users/{uid}/packingPlan has no document id; use
#   users/{uid}/packingPlan/current, matching the identity single-doc pattern.
# - The LOCKED taxonomy omits common room names; unmatched rooms use the early
#   decor/books bucket. Kitchen inventory is split by centralized essential keywords.
# - A one-day timeline cannot both keep first-night bag standalone and fit one session/day;
#   keep the bag standalone and co-schedule the final two tasks without putting both in dose.
#
